Subject: Adds an experimental register-bytecode backend and interpreter, guarded by `QJS_REGVM`

What this does
  Adds an experimental register-bytecode backend and interpreter, guarded by `QJS_REGVM`.

Why we need it
  The operand-stack interpreter pays a frame load and a frame store for every local and argument and a push and a pop for every temporary; a register form removes that traffic at the source, and this is the experiment that decides whether it beats the stack VM on the code react-native-quickjs runs.

What it adds
  `quickjs-regvm.h`, `js_regvm_scan`, `js_regvm_build_cfg`, `js_regvm_encode`, `js_regvm_execute`, and the three `builtin-*.regvm.h` blobs.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. It adds a serialized function tag; the final series-wide bump remains in 9999.
